{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Schrodinger's Cat Machine",
  "description": "THE SCHRODINGER'S CAT EXPERIMENT\n\nInside this mysterious box, a cat exists in quantum superposition - \nsimultaneously ALIVE and DEAD until observed!\n\nTHE SETUP:\nA single qubit is prepared in the state |psi> = (|0> + |1>) / sqrt(2)\nThis is a perfect 50/50 superposition.\n\n|0> = Cat is ALIVE (cartoon cat emerges)\n|1> = Cat is DEAD (adorable ghost-cat emerges)\n\nUntil you press the COLLAPSE button, the cat exists in BOTH states!\nThe qubit remains in superposition, neither alive nor dead.\n\nWHEN YOU PRESS COLLAPSE:\nThe quantum measurement occurs. The wavefunction collapses.\nThe universe \"decides\" - and one outcome becomes real.\n\nWHAT MAKES THIS SPECIAL:\nThis isn't pseudo-random. The IBM_QUANTUM node uses quantum mechanics -\ntrue quantum indeterminacy that even the universe doesn't \"know\" \nuntil measurement. Einstein hated this (\"God doesn't play dice!\").\nBut experiments prove: reality IS probabilistic at the quantum level.\n\nPHILOSOPHICAL IMPLICATIONS:\n- Does the cat experience both lives before collapse?\n- Does YOUR observation cause the collapse?\n- Are there parallel universes where the other outcome occurred?\n\nPress the button. Collapse the wavefunction. Meet your cat.\nEither way, they're very glad to see you.",
